#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""cc-pulse — the box's one status feed: one small JSON that every dashboard reads instead of collecting for itself.

WHY. cc-live, the web dashboard and the VR scene each walked /proc, parsed the boards and asked the laptop on their
own, and cc-live did it inside its key loop, so a keypress froze for 2-4 s behind a laptop ssh. Here one producer
keeps the status in memory, re-reads an input only when its mtime moves, and the views draw from that. The owner
asked for it on 2026-10-04 ("on main screen just see session and worker status", "maximally fast"); the design is
the planning seat's dashboard-design-2026-10-04.md.

  cc-pulse --once --json   print one snapshot as JSON (the shape below); --once never asks the laptop
  cc-pulse --once --text   print the main screen as text, 80x24 (what `cc-live --once` prints)
  cc-pulse run [--out F]   keep F (default $CC_STATE/pulse.json) current: written atomically (tmp file, then
                           rename) within ~50 ms of a change to a file it reads (inotify; a log written beside
                           one sets nothing off), and once a second anyway for /proc and the load; nothing else
                           polls. No unit runs it yet.
  cc-pulse selfcheck       cases over fixtures in a temp dir; reads nothing of the box's

THE SHAPE (`v` is 1; PR 2's /api/pulse and PR 3's VR read it, so a change here is a change to them):
  {v, at, zone, host,
   glance: {needs:{n}, sessions:{busy, waiting, idle, shell}, workers:{live, offline, held},
            landing:{active, queued, landed_1h}, box:{load1, cores, mem_pct, disk_pct, temp_c, units_down},
            limit_until, model, laptop, spend_today, members:{workspaces, sessions, rows, needs}},
   sessions: [{id, name, repo, track, state, since_s, ctx_pct, win}],     attention first: waiting, busy, shell, idle
   workers:  [{repo, track, title, status, live, moved_s, held}],          board rows marked running
   landing:  [{repo, pr, stage, title, age_s}],
   needs:    [{kind, repo, name, ask}],                                    kind pr | waiting | blocked | ask
   recent:   [{at, what, repo, name, title}],                              24 h of hand-offs and landings, cap 20
   projects: [{repo, live, running, open, needs, landed_at, usd, panel}],  one per board the box runs
   panels:   {repo: {title, at, rows:[{label, value, state}], stale, err}},
   sections: {name: {at, err, stale}}}
  Ages are seconds at `at`; times are epoch seconds. A section that raised keeps its last value and names the error
  under sections: `at` stays the time of its last good pass and `stale` is true, and the text views head that block
  STALE with that time (UNAVAILABLE when it never collected), so a retained row never reads as current. It holds no pane text, notes or mail, and a member's workspace only as the counts in
  glance.members, because PR 2 serves it on the internet behind the owner's gate.

WHAT IT READS — records the box already keeps, each re-parsed only when its mtime moves:
  sessions  ~/.claude/sessions/<pid>.json ($CC_SESSIONS), only when that pid is alive with the same start time
            (procStart; a record with none only when the pid is a claude started before the record was written);
            context % from $CC_STATE/statusline/<sessionId>.json, read on the 1 s tick and not watched (a busy
            session writes it several times a second); agent_no, the box's number for it (cc-agent-number), from the
            CC_AGENT_NO in /proc/<pid>/environ, else the ledger's latest line for that pid ($CC_AGENT_LEDGER, default
            $CC_STATE/agent-numbers.jsonl), which a session no launcher numbered got on its first tool call.
  workers   boards ($CC_BOARDS or ~/.cc/boards/<repo>.json, `_` boards skipped): rows marked running, not
            kind=session. One /proc pass a second: a `cc-loop <repo> <track>` argv, or a `claude` whose cwd is under
            the worktrees root ($CC_WORKTREES), makes that track LIVE; a row whose `agent` mark names a live pid is
            worked by a SESSION; a `held` row is HELD; any other is OFFLINE (marked running, nothing alive), so the
            pulse shows no phantom work. A live worker's last move is the newer mtime of its loop.log or progress.md.
  landing   $CC_LANDER_STATE (default $CC_STATE/land)/*.json, the in-flight jobs; queue.log, read on from where the
            last pass stopped, says when each PR landed (a `stage R#N merged` or `notify R#N landed` line).
  needs     $CC_STATE/home.json, cc-slack's own rule (home_needs): owed PR reviews, waiting or blocked tracks that
            carry a reason, and a session's declared ask. units_down and spend come from there too.
  box       /proc/loadavg, /proc/meminfo and the home disk each second; temp from $CC_STATE/vitals/current.json.
  slow      $CC_STATE/reconcile.json limit_until; $CC_STATE/model-override's model (never `cc-model status`);
            `cc-suites status --quick`'s lines for the laptop (its answer, then its GPU's stats; --quick, so Blender
            is never started there), once a minute in a thread of its own so nothing waits on it.
  members   ~/.cc/members/<repo> ($CC_MEMBERS) or ~/dev/<repo>/.cc/member-facing ($CC_DEV) makes <repo> a
            member's: counted, never named.

A PROJECT'S OWN PANEL. Any project can show its own numbers (the fund: paper P&L, positions, data freshness) by
writing $CC_STATE/<repo>/panel.json, at most 4096 bytes (aim for 2 KB):
    {"title": "fund", "at": "2026-10-05T08:00:00Z", "stale_after": 600,
     "rows": [{"label": "paper P&L", "value": "+$212 (1.4%)", "state": "ok"}, ...]}
  `state` is ok, warn or bad (anything else shows plain); at most 20 rows; a label is cut to 24 characters, a
  value to 40, the title to 40. `stale_after` defaults to 600 s. cc-pulse owns the frame and the project owns only
  its panel: a panel that is too big, not JSON or the wrong shape carries `err` and no rows, one older than
  stale_after is marked stale, and neither touches anything else. A member's workspace gets no panel. Write it
  atomically (tmp file, then rename), so a reader never sees half of it.
"""
import calendar
import ctypes
import ctypes.util
import glob
import json
import os
import select
import shutil
import stat
import struct
import subprocess
import sys
import threading
import time

HOME = os.path.expanduser("~")
V = 1
RECENT = 86400            # hand-offs and landings in `recent` go back this far ...
RECENT_CAP = 20           # ... at most this many
AMBER = 30                # a pulse older than this shows its age in amber ...
STALE = 90                # ... and older than this says STALE: the producer is down
SLOW = 60                 # the laptop is asked this often
PANEL_MAX = 4096
READ_MAX = 64 << 20     # no input is read past this (the biggest board is ~3.4 MB)
# recurring-defect-ok: pause-hold-missing — cc-pulse only reads state and writes its own pulse file; it launches no worker and writes no board
BOARD_MAX = 4 << 20     # a board is read to this size at most
OPEN = ("queued", "running", "review", "blocked", "waiting", "held")
ORDER = {"waiting": 0, "busy": 1, "shell": 2, "idle": 3}


def env(k, default):
    return os.environ.get(k) or default


def boards_dir():
    return env("CC_BOARDS", f"{HOME}/.cc/boards")


def state_dir():
    return env("CC_STATE", f"{HOME}/.cc/state")


def land_dir():
    return env("CC_LANDER_STATE", f"{state_dir()}/land")


def wt_root():
    return env("CC_WORKTREES", f"{HOME}/.cc/worktrees")


def sessions_dir():
    return env("CC_SESSIONS", f"{HOME}/.claude/sessions")


def out_path():
    return env("CC_PULSE", f"{state_dir()}/pulse.json")


def ts(s):
    """An ISO stamp the board writes (2026-09-28T19:31:30Z) as epoch seconds, or 0."""
    if not isinstance(s, str):  # a project's panel can put anything here
        return 0
    try:                       # sliced, not strptime: a cold start reads thousands of these
        if len(s) == 20 and s[4] == s[7] == "-" and s[10] == "T" and s[19] == "Z":
            return calendar.timegm((int(s[:4]), int(s[5:7]), int(s[8:10]), int(s[11:13]), int(s[14:16]),
                                    int(s[17:19]), 0, 0, 0))
    except (TypeError, ValueError):
        pass
    return 0


def mtime(p):
    try:
        return os.stat(p).st_mtime
    except OSError:
        return 0


def ago(sec):
    sec = max(0, int(sec or 0))
    for unit, div in (("d", 86400), ("h", 3600), ("m", 60)):
        if sec >= div:
            return f"{sec // div}{unit}"
    return f"{sec}s"


_C = {}


def read_capped(path, cap=READ_MAX):
    """A regular file's bytes, or None when it is missing, not a regular file or over `cap` bytes. A member's board
    is a symlink into a directory its sandbox writes, so it may point at a FIFO (open would block the collector) or
    /dev/zero (read would never end): the open never blocks and fstat refuses both."""
    try:
        fd = os.open(path, os.O_RDONLY | os.O_NONBLOCK | os.O_CLOEXEC)
    except OSError:
        return None
    try:
        if not stat.S_ISREG(os.fstat(fd).st_mode):
            return None
        with os.fdopen(fd, "rb", closefd=False) as f:
            b = f.read(cap + 1)
        return b if len(b) <= cap else None
    except OSError:
        return None
    finally:
        os.close(fd)


def cached(path, parse=None, cap=READ_MAX):
    """The parsed file, parsed again only when its mtime moves; None when it is missing, not a regular file, over
    cap bytes or does not parse (too deeply nested counts as not parsing)."""
    m = mtime(path)
    hit = _C.get(path)
    if hit and hit[0] == m:
        return hit[1]
    v = None
    if m:
        b = read_capped(path, cap)
        try:
            v = (parse or json.loads)(b) if b is not None else None
        except (ValueError, RecursionError, MemoryError):
            v = None
    _C[path] = (m, v)
    return v


_MEMBER = {"at": 0, "is": {}}


def is_member(repo):
    """Whether <repo> is a member's workspace; each answer is kept for 10 s, so a pass stats each repo once."""
    if time.monotonic() - _MEMBER["at"] > 10:
        _MEMBER.update(at=time.monotonic(), **{"is": {}})
    if repo not in _MEMBER["is"]:
        _MEMBER["is"][repo] = bool(repo) and (
            os.path.isdir(f"{env('CC_MEMBERS', HOME + '/.cc/members')}/{repo}")
            or os.path.isfile(f"{env('CC_DEV', HOME + '/dev')}/{repo}/.cc/member-facing"))
    return _MEMBER["is"][repo]


def boards():
    """{repo: tracks} for every real board, members' included (callers count those and name none)."""
    out = {}
    for path in sorted(glob.glob(f"{boards_dir()}/*.json")):
        repo = os.path.basename(path)[:-5]
        if repo.startswith("_"):
            continue
        d = cached(path, cap=BOARD_MAX)
        t = d.get("tracks") if isinstance(d, dict) else None
        out[repo] = {k: r for k, r in t.items() if isinstance(r, dict)} if isinstance(t, dict) else {}
    return out


# The commands whose argv can carry `cc-loop <repo> <track>`. cc-loop is a bash script, so the loop itself is `bash`
# (its tmux window's shell is bash or sh); `cc … --go` starts it as `cc-room admit <repo/track> … -- cc-loop <repo>
# <track>`, and cc-room is a python3 script, so python3 is read too or a loop waiting for its room shows OFFLINE.
WORKER_COMMS = ("bash", "sh", "cc-loop", "claude", "python3")


def procs(proc="/proc"):
    """(live tracks {repo/track}, live pids) from one pass over /proc; argv is read only for the few commands that
    can be a worker, and cwd only for claude."""
    live, pids, root = set(), set(), wt_root().rstrip("/") + "/"
    for pid in os.listdir(proc):
        if not pid.isdigit():
            continue
        pids.add(pid)
        try:
            comm = open(f"{proc}/{pid}/comm").read().strip()
            if comm not in WORKER_COMMS:
                continue
            argv = open(f"{proc}/{pid}/cmdline", "rb").read().decode("utf-8", "replace").split("\0")
        except OSError:
            continue
        for i, a in enumerate(argv):
            # cc-loop is the program or the script it runs (argv[0] or argv[1]), or the word after cc-room's `--`; a
            # later word with that basename is someone else's argument (`python3 tool.py core/bin/cc-loop a b`)
            if os.path.basename(a) == "cc-loop" and (i <= 1 or argv[i - 1] == "--") and len(argv) > i + 2 and argv[i + 1] and argv[i + 2]:
                live.add(f"{argv[i + 1]}/{argv[i + 2]}")
                break
        if comm == "claude":
            try:
                cwd = os.readlink(f"{proc}/{pid}/cwd")
            except OSError:
                continue
            if cwd.startswith(root):
                live.add("/".join(cwd[len(root):].split("/")[:2]))
    return live, pids


def where(cwd):
    """(repo, track) a session works in, from its cwd: a worktree is both, ~/dev/<repo> is the repo's seat."""
    cwd = str(cwd or "")
    for root, n in ((wt_root().rstrip("/") + "/", 2), (env("CC_DEV", HOME + "/dev").rstrip("/") + "/", 1)):
        if cwd.startswith(root):
            parts = cwd[len(root):].split("/")[:n] + [""]
            return parts[0], parts[1] if n == 2 else ""
    return "", ""


def started(proc, pid):
    """The pid's start time in clock ticks (/proc/<pid>/stat field 22), or None when it is gone."""
    try:
        return open(f"{proc}/{pid}/stat").read().rpartition(")")[2].split()[19]
    except (OSError, IndexError):
        return None


def booted(proc):
    """The boot time in epoch seconds (/proc/stat's btime), or None."""
    try:
        for ln in open(f"{proc}/stat"):
            if ln.startswith("btime "):
                return int(ln.split()[1])
    except (OSError, ValueError, IndexError):
        pass
    return None


def same_process(proc, pid, d):
    """Whether pid is still the process that wrote session record d. Claude Code writes procStart as /proc/<pid>/stat
    field 22 in a decimal string ("69115728" on 2.1.296, read off a live file on 2026-10-10); it is compared as a
    number, so 69115728, "69115728" and "69115728.0" are one value. A record with no usable procStart (an older
    Claude Code) is believed only when the pid is a `claude` process that started no later than the record's own
    first stamp, so a pid reused by anything else, or by a later claude, is not a live session."""
    st = started(proc, pid)
    if st is None:
        return False
    try:
        want = int(float(str(d.get("procStart")).strip()))
    except (TypeError, ValueError, OverflowError):
        want = None
    if want is not None:
        return str(want) == st
    try:
        if open(f"{proc}/{pid}/comm").read().strip() != "claude":
            return False
    except OSError:
        return False
    stamps = [v for v in (d.get(k) for k in ("startedAt", "updatedAt", "statusUpdatedAt"))
              if isinstance(v, (int, float)) and not isinstance(v, bool) and v > 0]
    boot = booted(proc)
    if not stamps or boot is None:
        return False
    try:
        born = boot + int(st) / (os.sysconf("SC_CLK_TCK") or 100)
    except ValueError:
        return False
    return born <= min(stamps) / 1000 + 2       # 2 s for the clock tick and btime's rounding


def agent_no(proc, pid):
    """The number the box gave this session (cc-agent-number), from the CC_AGENT_NO its spawner set, or None."""
    try:
        with open(f"{proc}/{pid}/environ", "rb") as f:
            env = f.read().split(b"\0")
    except OSError:
        return None
    return next((e[12:].decode("utf-8", "replace") for e in env if e.startswith(b"CC_AGENT_NO=") and e[12:]), None)


def ledger_nos(proc):
    """{pid: number} from the agent ledger, the latest line for each pid winning; {} when it cannot be read. A line
    whose recorded start time is not the live process's was written for an earlier holder of a reused pid, and is
    skipped."""
    out = {}
    try:
        with open(env("CC_AGENT_LEDGER", f"{state_dir()}/agent-numbers.jsonl"), errors="replace") as f:
            for line in f:
                try:
                    d = json.loads(line)
                    if d.get("start") in (None, started(proc, d["pid"])):
                        out[str(d["pid"])] = str(d["id"])
                except (ValueError, KeyError, TypeError):
                    pass
    except OSError:
        pass
    return out


def sessions(now, proc="/proc"):
    """([session], member sessions) of every Claude session whose process is still the one that wrote its file."""
    out, members, nos = [], 0, ledger_nos(proc)
    for path in glob.glob(f"{sessions_dir()}/*.json"):
        pid = os.path.basename(path)[:-5]
        d = cached(path)
        if not pid.isdigit() or not isinstance(d, dict):
            continue
        if not same_process(proc, pid, d):
            continue
        repo, track = where(d.get("cwd"))
        if is_member(repo):
            members += 1
            continue
        sl = cached(f"{state_dir()}/statusline/{d.get('sessionId')}.json") if d.get("sessionId") else None
        since = (d.get("statusUpdatedAt") or d.get("updatedAt") or 0) / 1000
        win = str(d.get("tmux") or "").partition(":")[2].partition(".")[0]
        out.append({"id": pid, "name": str(d.get("name") or pid)[:40], "repo": repo, "track": track,
                    "state": str(d.get("status") or "?"), "since_s": int(now - since) if since else None,
                    "ctx_pct": sl.get("pct") if isinstance(sl, dict) else None, "win": win,
                    "agent_no": agent_no(proc, pid) or nos.get(pid)})
    out.sort(key=lambda s: (ORDER.get(s["state"], 2), s["since_s"] if s["since_s"] is not None else 1e12))
    return out, members


def workers(bds, live, pids, now):
    """([worker], member rows running) of the board rows marked running."""
    out, members = [], 0
    for repo, tracks in sorted(bds.items()):
        for name, row in sorted(tracks.items()):
            if row.get("status") != "running" or row.get("kind") == "session":
                continue
            if is_member(repo):
                members += 1
                continue
            key, moved = f"{repo}/{name}", None
            if key in live:
                d = f"{state_dir()}/{repo}/{name}"
                last = max(mtime(f"{d}/loop.log"), mtime(f"{d}/progress.md"))
                word, moved = "live", int(now - last) if last else None
            elif str(row.get("agent") or "").rpartition(":")[2] in pids:   # `agent me`: a live session works it itself
                word = "session"
            elif row.get("held"):          # a person parked it on purpose: not an alarm
                word = "held"
            else:
                word = "offline"
            out.append({"repo": repo, "track": name, "title": str(row.get("title") or "")[:80], "status": "running",
                        "live": word, "moved_s": moved, "held": bool(row.get("held"))})
    out.sort(key=lambda w: ("offline", "live", "session", "held").index(w["live"]))    # attention first
    return out, members


_LOG = {"ino": None, "off": 0, "landed": {}, "sorted": []}
_LOG_LOCK = threading.Lock()   # the feed thread and cc-live's deeper views both call landed()


def landed():
    """[(epoch, repo, pr)] of every PR the queue log says landed, newest first. The log is read on from the offset the
    last call stopped at; a log that was replaced or cut short is read again from the top."""
    with _LOG_LOCK:
        return _landed()


def _landed():
    path = f"{land_dir()}/queue.log"
    try:
        st = os.stat(path)
    except OSError:
        return []
    if st.st_ino != _LOG["ino"] or st.st_size < _LOG["off"]:
        _LOG.update(ino=st.st_ino, off=0, landed={}, sorted=[])
    if st.st_size > _LOG["off"]:
        with open(path, "rb") as f:
            f.seek(_LOG["off"])
            data = f.read()
        cut = data.rfind(b"\n") + 1            # a half-written last line is read whole next time
        _LOG["off"] += cut
        for ln in data[:cut].decode("utf-8", "replace").splitlines():
            if " merged" not in ln and " landed" not in ln:
                continue
            stamp, _, rest = ln.partition("\t")
            w = rest.split()
            if len(w) < 3 or (w[0], w[2]) not in (("stage", "merged"), ("notify", "landed")):
                continue
            repo, _, pr = w[1].rpartition("#")
            when = ts(stamp)
            if repo and not repo.startswith("_") and pr.isdigit() and when:
                k = (repo, pr)
                _LOG["landed"][k] = min(when, _LOG["landed"].get(k, when))
        _LOG["sorted"] = sorted(((t, r, p) for (r, p), t in _LOG["landed"].items()), reverse=True)
    return _LOG["sorted"]


def job(repo, pr):
    """The lander's record of repo#pr, in flight or ended, or {}."""
    for path in (f"{land_dir()}/{repo}-{pr}.json", f"{land_dir()}/rest/{repo}-{pr}.json"):
        j = cached(path)
        if isinstance(j, dict):
            return j
    return {}


def landing(now):
    """[landing] in flight, newest first, members' left out."""
    out = []
    for path in glob.glob(f"{land_dir()}/*.json"):
        j = cached(path)
        if isinstance(j, dict) and j.get("repo") and j.get("pr") and not is_member(j["repo"]):
            out.append({"repo": j["repo"], "pr": j["pr"], "stage": str(j.get("stage") or j.get("state") or "?"),
                        "title": str(j.get("title") or "")[:80], "age_s": int(now - mtime(path))})
    return sorted(out, key=lambda e: e["age_s"])


def home_state():
    d = cached(f"{state_dir()}/home.json")
    s = d.get("state") if isinstance(d, dict) else None
    return s if isinstance(s, dict) else {}


def needs(hs):
    """([need], member needs) by cc-slack's home_needs rule, from the home.json it already writes."""
    out, members = [], 0

    def add(rank, kind, repo, name, ask):
        nonlocal members
        if is_member(repo):
            members += 1
        else:
            out.append((rank, {"kind": kind, "repo": repo, "name": str(name or "")[:40], "ask": str(ask or "")[:80]}))
    for t in hs.get("tracks") or ():
        if not isinstance(t, dict):
            continue
        repo, _, name = str(t.get("name") or "").partition("/")
        pr = t.get("pr") if isinstance(t.get("pr"), dict) else {}
        owed = bool(pr.get("num") and pr.get("owed") and t.get("state") in ("review", "done"))
        asks = t.get("state") in ("waiting", "blocked") and bool(t.get("reason"))
        # Whose track it is comes from the track's own name, the way workers() and recent() decide, and is settled
        # before anything of its PR is read: a member's track is a count, whatever repo its PR record claims.
        if is_member(repo) or (owed and is_member(str(pr.get("repo") or "").rpartition("/")[2])):
            members += owed + asks
            continue
        if owed:
            add(1, "pr", str(pr.get("repo") or repo), f"PR #{pr['num']}", "awaiting review")
        if asks:
            add(2 if t["state"] == "waiting" else 3, t["state"], repo, name, t.get("reason"))
    for s in hs.get("sessions") or ():
        if isinstance(s, dict) and s.get("ask"):
            add(2, "ask", s.get("repo") or "", s.get("name"), s.get("ask"))
    return [n for _, n in sorted(out, key=lambda e: e[0])], members


def handoff(row):
    """(when, word) of a row's newest hand-off: added, dispatched (a worker went out) or taken (an agent mark)."""
    ev = [(ts(row.get("created")), "added")]
    for n in row.get("notes") or []:
        if isinstance(n, dict) and str(n.get("msg", "")).startswith("dispatched"):
            ev.append((ts(n.get("ts")), "dispatched"))
    if row.get("agent_at"):
        ev.append((ts(row.get("agent_at")), "taken"))
    return max(ev)


def recent(bds, ld, now):
    out = []
    for repo, tracks in bds.items():
        if is_member(repo):
            continue
        for name, row in tracks.items():
            when, word = handoff(row)
            if when and 0 <= now - when <= RECENT:
                out.append({"at": when, "what": word, "repo": repo, "name": name,
                            "title": str(row.get("title") or "")[:80]})
    for when, repo, pr in ld:
        if now - when > RECENT:
            break
        if not is_member(repo):
            out.append({"at": when, "what": "landed", "repo": repo, "name": f"#{pr}",
                        "title": str(job(repo, pr).get("title") or "")[:80]})
    return sorted(out, key=lambda e: -e["at"])[:RECENT_CAP]


def box(hs):
    """The load, memory and disk now, the temperature off cc-vitals' last minute and the units home.json saw down."""
    out = {"load1": None, "cores": os.cpu_count(), "mem_pct": None, "disk_pct": None, "temp_c": None,
           "units_down": sum(1 for u in hs.get("units") or () if isinstance(u, list) and len(u) > 1 and not u[1])}
    try:
        out["load1"] = float(open("/proc/loadavg").read().split()[0])
        mi = {ln.split(":")[0]: int(ln.split()[1]) for ln in open("/proc/meminfo") if ln.split()[1:2]}
        out["mem_pct"] = round(100 * (1 - mi["MemAvailable"] / mi["MemTotal"]))
    except (OSError, ValueError, KeyError, ZeroDivisionError):
        pass
    try:
        du = shutil.disk_usage(HOME)
        out["disk_pct"] = round(100 * du.used / du.total)
    except OSError:
        pass
    vit = cached(f"{state_dir()}/vitals/current.json")
    for s in (vit or {}).get("series") or () if isinstance(vit, dict) else ():
        if isinstance(s, dict) and s.get("key") == "temp" and isinstance(s.get("now"), dict):
            out["temp_c"] = num(s["now"].get("real"))
    return out


def num(v):
    """v as a float, or None when it is not a number (a reading another tool wrote can be anything)."""
    try:
        f = float(v)
    except (TypeError, ValueError, OverflowError):
        return None
    return f if f == f and abs(f) != float("inf") else None


def limit_until(now):
    d = cached(f"{state_dir()}/reconcile.json")
    try:
        v = float(d.get("limit_until") or 0)
    except (AttributeError, TypeError, ValueError):
        return None
    return v if v > now else None


def model(now):
    """The model the box was moved to (cc-model's override file: model, since, until, …), or "default"."""
    ov = cached(f"{state_dir()}/model-override", lambda b: b.decode("utf-8", "replace"))
    f = (ov or "").strip().split("\t")
    try:
        until = float(f[2]) if len(f) > 2 and f[2] else 0
    except ValueError:
        until = 0
    return f[0] if f[0] and (not until or until > now) else "default"


def laptop_line():
    """cc-suites status --quick's lines (the answer, the GPU's stats), one per line, or one saying the runner gave none;
    never waits more than 6 s. --quick: plain status starts Blender on the laptop, which outlasts the 6 s."""
    exe = env("CC_PULSE_SUITES", os.path.join(os.path.dirname(os.path.realpath(__file__)), "cc-suites"))
    try:
        r = subprocess.run([exe, "status", "--quick"], capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=6,
                           stdin=subprocess.DEVNULL, env={**os.environ, "CC_SUITES_STATUS_TIMEOUT": "5s"})
        return "\n".join(ln[:120] for ln in (r.stdout.strip().splitlines() or ["cc-suites status printed nothing"]))
    except (OSError, subprocess.SubprocessError):
        return "the laptop runner did not answer in 6 s"


def panel(path, now):
    """One project's panel.json, checked: the panel, or one carrying `err` and no rows."""
    if os.path.getsize(path) > PANEL_MAX:
        return {"title": "", "at": None, "rows": [], "stale": False, "err": f"over {PANEL_MAX} bytes"}
    d = cached(path)
    if not isinstance(d, dict) or not isinstance(d.get("rows"), list):
        return {"title": "", "at": None, "rows": [], "stale": False, "err": "not a panel: no rows list"}
    if d.get("at") is not None and not isinstance(d["at"], str):
        return {"title": "", "at": None, "rows": [], "stale": False, "err": "not a panel: at is not a time string"}
    at = ts(d.get("at"))
    try:
        after = float(d.get("stale_after") or 600)
    except (TypeError, ValueError, OverflowError):
        after = 600
    rows = [{"label": str(r.get("label") or "")[:24], "value": str(r.get("value") if r.get("value") is not None else "")[:40],
             "state": r.get("state") if r.get("state") in ("ok", "warn", "bad") else ""}
            for r in d["rows"][:20] if isinstance(r, dict)]
    return {"title": str(d.get("title") or "")[:40], "at": at or None, "rows": rows,
            "stale": not at or now - at > after, "err": None}


def panels(now):
    """{repo: panel}; one panel that fails carries its own err, and every other panel is still read."""
    out = {}
    for path in sorted(glob.glob(f"{state_dir()}/*/panel.json")):
        repo = path.split("/")[-2]
        if not repo.startswith("_") and not is_member(repo):
            try:
                out[repo] = panel(path, now)
            except OSError:
                continue
            except Exception as e:     # a project's own file never takes the other panels down
                out[repo] = {"title": "", "at": None, "rows": [], "stale": False,
                             "err": f"unreadable: {type(e).__name__}"[:60]}
    return out


def projects(bds, wk, nd, ld, hs, pn):
    """One row per board the box runs (members' counted in glance.members instead)."""
    spend = {}
    for r in ((hs.get("spend") or {}).get("rows") or ()) if isinstance(hs.get("spend"), dict) else ():
        if isinstance(r, dict) and "/" in str(r.get("who")) and isinstance(r.get("usd"), (int, float)):
            k = str(r["who"]).partition("/")[0]
            spend[k] = spend.get(k, 0) + r["usd"]
    last = {}
    for when, repo, _ in ld:
        last.setdefault(repo, when)
    out = []
    for repo, tracks in sorted(bds.items()):
        if is_member(repo):
            continue
        st = [r.get("status") for r in tracks.values()]
        out.append({"repo": repo, "live": sum(1 for w in wk if w["repo"] == repo and w["live"] in ("live", "session")),
                    "running": st.count("running"), "open": sum(1 for s in st if s in OPEN),
                    "needs": sum(1 for n in nd if n["repo"] == repo), "landed_at": last.get(repo),
                    "usd": round(spend[repo], 2) if repo in spend else None, "panel": repo in pn})
    return out


class Pulse:
    """The snapshot, kept in memory. step() re-collects; each section runs on its own, and one that raises keeps its
    last value with its error under sections. /proc is walked only when `walk` is set (the 1 s tick)."""

    def __init__(self, proc="/proc"):
        self.proc, self.p, self.live, self.pids = proc, {}, set(), set()
        self.laptop, self.laptop_at, self.asking = None, 0, False
        self.sec, self.last = {}, {}

    def run_sec(self, name, fn, default):
        try:
            v = self.last[name] = fn()
            self.sec[name] = {"at": int(time.time()), "err": None, "stale": False}
            return v
        except Exception as e:     # one bad input greys out its own section, never the rest
            # what it shows is the last pass that worked: `at` says when that was, and `stale` that it is not now
            self.sec[name] = {"at": (self.sec.get(name) or {}).get("at"), "err": f"{type(e).__name__}: {e}"[:120],
                              "stale": name in self.last}
            return self.last.get(name, default)

    def ask_laptop(self):
        """Ask the laptop in a thread of its own, at most once a minute; the pulse never waits on the answer."""
        if self.asking or time.time() - self.laptop_at < SLOW:
            return
        self.asking = True

        def go():
            try:
                self.laptop = laptop_line()
            finally:
                self.laptop_at, self.asking = time.time(), False
        threading.Thread(target=go, daemon=True).start()

    def step(self, now=None, walk=True, laptop=True, quick=False):
        """The snapshot now. `quick` leaves the landing history, recent, projects and panels at their last value (none,
        on a first step) so a view can draw sessions and workers first; the next step fills them in."""
        now = now or time.time()
        slow = (lambda name, fn, default: self.last.get(name, default)) if quick else self.run_sec
        if walk or not self.pids:
            self.live, self.pids = self.run_sec("procs", lambda: procs(self.proc), (set(), set()))
        if laptop:
            self.ask_laptop()
        bds = self.run_sec("boards", boards, {})
        hs = self.run_sec("home", home_state, {})
        ss, s_mem = self.run_sec("sessions", lambda: sessions(now, self.proc), ([], 0))
        wk, _ = self.run_sec("workers", lambda: workers(bds, self.live, self.pids, now), ([], 0))
        ld = slow("landed", landed, [])
        lg = slow("landing", lambda: landing(now), [])
        nd, n_mem = self.run_sec("needs", lambda: needs(hs), ([], 0))
        pn = slow("panels", lambda: panels(now), {})
        members = [r for r in bds if is_member(r)]
        spend = hs.get("spend") if isinstance(hs.get("spend"), dict) else {}
        count = lambda xs, k, v: sum(1 for x in xs if x[k] == v)
        self.p = {
            "v": V, "at": int(now), "zone": time.strftime("%Z"), "host": os.uname().nodename,
            "glance": {
                "needs": {"n": len(nd)},
                "sessions": {w: count(ss, "state", w) for w in ("busy", "waiting", "idle", "shell")},
                "workers": {"live": sum(1 for w in wk if w["live"] in ("live", "session")),
                            "offline": count(wk, "live", "offline"), "held": count(wk, "live", "held")},
                "landing": {"active": sum(1 for x in lg if x["stage"] not in ("queued", "install")),
                            "queued": count(lg, "stage", "queued"),
                            "landed_1h": sum(1 for t, _, _ in ld if now - t <= 3600)},
                "box": self.run_sec("box", lambda: box(hs), {}),
                "limit_until": self.run_sec("limit", lambda: limit_until(now), None),
                "model": self.run_sec("model", lambda: model(now), None),
                "laptop": self.laptop,
                "spend_today": round(spend["today"], 2) if isinstance(spend.get("today"), (int, float)) else None,
                "members": {"workspaces": len(members), "sessions": s_mem, "needs": n_mem,
                            "rows": sum(1 for r in members for x in bds[r].values() if x.get("status") in OPEN)}},
            "sessions": ss, "workers": wk, "landing": lg, "needs": nd,
            "recent": slow("recent", lambda: recent(bds, ld, now), []),
            "projects": slow("projects", lambda: projects(bds, wk, nd, ld, hs, pn), []),
            "panels": pn, "sections": dict(self.sec)}
        return self.p


# ── watching: inotify through libc, no package ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
IN_MODIFY, IN_CLOSE_WRITE, IN_MOVED_FROM, IN_MOVED_TO, IN_CREATE, IN_DELETE = 0x2, 0x8, 0x40, 0x80, 0x100, 0x200
WATCH = IN_CLOSE_WRITE | IN_MOVED_FROM | IN_MOVED_TO | IN_CREATE | IN_DELETE | IN_MODIFY


class Watch:
    """inotify on a set of directories. wait(t) returns the names that changed within t seconds (empty on timeout).
    With no inotify (another OS, or the watch limit reached) it only sleeps, and callers fall back to their tick."""

    def __init__(self):
        self.fd, self.dirs = -1, {}
        try:
            self.libc = ctypes.CDLL(ctypes.util.find_library("c") or "libc.so.6", use_errno=True)
            self.fd = self.libc.inotify_init1(os.O_NONBLOCK | os.O_CLOEXEC)
        except (OSError, AttributeError):
            self.fd = -1

    def add(self, path):
        if self.fd < 0 or path in self.dirs.values() or not os.path.isdir(path):
            return
        wd = self.libc.inotify_add_watch(self.fd, os.fsencode(path), WATCH)
        if wd >= 0:
            self.dirs[wd] = path

    def close(self):
        if self.fd >= 0:
            os.close(self.fd)
        self.fd, self.dirs = -1, {}

    def wait(self, timeout):
        if self.fd < 0:
            time.sleep(max(0, timeout))
            return set()
        if not select.select([self.fd], [], [], max(0, timeout))[0]:
            return set()
        got = set()
        while True:
            try:
                buf = os.read(self.fd, 65536)
            except BlockingIOError:
                return got
            i = 0
            while i + 16 <= len(buf):
                wd, _, _, n = struct.unpack_from("iIII", buf, i)
                name = buf[i + 16:i + 16 + n].rstrip(b"\0").decode("utf-8", "replace")
                got.add(os.path.join(self.dirs.get(wd, ""), name))
                i += 16 + n


QUIET = ("statusline",)   # written every few hundred ms by a busy session; the 1 s tick picks up its context %


def inputs():
    """The directories whose files the pulse reads: a write in any of them re-collects at once."""
    st = state_dir()
    return [boards_dir(), sessions_dir(), land_dir(), f"{st}/vitals", st] + \
        sorted(d for d in glob.glob(f"{st}/*/") if not os.path.basename(d.rstrip("/")).startswith("_")
               and os.path.basename(d.rstrip("/")) not in QUIET)


TOP = ("home.json", "reconcile.json", "model-override")     # the files the pulse reads straight under $CC_STATE


def wanted(path):
    """Whether a write to `path` changes what the pulse shows. The watched directories also hold logs that grow all
    day ($CC_STATE's pulse.log, model.log and reconcile.log, a repo's loop.log); a write to one of those re-collects
    nothing, and a worker's last move is read on the 1 s tick instead."""
    d, n, st = os.path.dirname(path).rstrip("/"), os.path.basename(path), state_dir().rstrip("/")
    if d in (boards_dir().rstrip("/"), sessions_dir().rstrip("/")):
        return n.endswith(".json")
    if d == land_dir().rstrip("/"):
        return n.endswith(".json") or n == "queue.log"
    if d == f"{st}/vitals":
        return n == "current.json"
    if d == st:
        return n in TOP or (os.path.isdir(path) and not n.startswith("_") and n not in QUIET)
    return os.path.dirname(d) == st and n == "panel.json"


def feed(emit, stop=None, proc="/proc", settle=0.03, out=None):
    """Keep a Pulse current and hand each new snapshot to emit(p): within `settle` s of a write to a watched input
    (more writes in that window are taken together), and every second for /proc and the load. `out` is the file
    emit writes, if any (default the pulse file): a write to it or its tmp file is our own and re-collects nothing.
    Returns when stop() is true."""
    pulse, w = Pulse(proc), Watch()
    own = {os.path.realpath(x) for x in (out or out_path(), (out or out_path()) + ".tmp")}
    try:
        for d in inputs():
            w.add(d)
        emit(pulse.step(quick=True))          # sessions and workers on screen first ...
        emit(pulse.step(walk=False))          # ... and the landing history a moment later
        tick = time.monotonic()
        while not (stop and stop()):
            due = tick + 1 - time.monotonic()
            changed = w.wait(due)
            walk = time.monotonic() - tick >= 1
            if changed:
                time.sleep(settle)
                changed |= w.wait(0)
                for p in changed:
                    if os.path.dirname(p) == state_dir().rstrip("/") and os.path.isdir(p) \
                            and os.path.basename(p) not in QUIET:
                        w.add(p)       # a new project's state dir: its panel.json is watched from now on
                if not walk and not any(wanted(p) and os.path.realpath(p) not in own for p in changed):
                    continue           # our own write, or a log the pulse does not read
            elif not walk:
                continue
            if walk:
                tick = time.monotonic()
            emit(pulse.step(walk=walk))
    finally:
        w.close()


def write(p, path=None):
    path = path or out_path()
    tmp = f"{path}.tmp"
    with open(tmp, "w") as f:
        json.dump(p, f, separators=(",", ":"))
    os.replace(tmp, path)


# ── the text: the main screen, and the sections the pulse carries ─────────────────────────────────────────────
def age_line(p, now=None):
    a = int((now or time.time()) - (p.get("at") or 0))
    return (f"STALE {ago(a)}", "bad") if a > STALE else (f"pulse {ago(a)}", "warn" if a >= AMBER else "")


def header(p, now=None, width=80):
    g, now = p.get("glance") or {}, now or time.time()
    b = g.get("box") or {}
    f = lambda v, fmt: fmt.format(v) if v is not None else "?"
    bits = [p.get("host", "?"), time.strftime("%H:%M:%S", time.localtime(now)),
            f"ld {f(b.get('load1'), '{:.1f}')}/{b.get('cores') or '?'}", f"mem {f(b.get('mem_pct'), '{}%')}",
            f"disk {f(b.get('disk_pct'), '{}%')}"]
    if num(b.get("temp_c")) is not None:        # a pulse.json another writer made can carry anything here
        bits.append(f"{num(b['temp_c']):.0f}°C")
    if b.get("units_down"):
        bits.append(f"{b['units_down']} unit(s) DOWN")
    if g.get("spend_today") is not None:
        bits.append(f"${g['spend_today']:.0f} today")
    if g.get("model") and g["model"] != "default":
        bits.append(f"model {g['model']}")
    if g.get("limit_until"):
        bits.append(f"LIMIT to {time.strftime('%H:%M', time.localtime(g['limit_until']))}")
    word, tone = age_line(p, now)
    return [(cut("  ".join(bits), width - len(word) - 2) + "  " + word, tone or ("bad" if b.get("units_down") else ""))]


# The sections each block of the screen is drawn from: when one of them failed, the block shows a retained value.
FEEDS = {"sessions": ("sessions",), "workers": ("workers", "procs", "boards"), "needs": ("needs", "home"),
         "landing": ("landing",)}


def stale_note(p, block):
    """'' while every section a block is drawn from collected on the last pass; else what the owner must know: that
    the rows are the last good pass's (and when it was), or that there is none."""
    sec = p.get("sections") or {}
    for name in FEEDS.get(block, (block,)):
        s = sec.get(name) or {}
        if s.get("err"):
            at = s.get("at")
            return (f"STALE: as of {time.strftime('%H:%M:%S', time.localtime(at))}, {name} failed (x: why)" if at
                    else f"UNAVAILABLE: {name} failed (x: why)")
    return ""


def block_head(p, block, head, rest, width):
    """A block's heading as (text, tone): `head` (its name and count), then its stale note when it has one, so the
    note is never the part an 80-column cut drops, then `rest`."""
    note = stale_note(p, block)
    return (cut("  ".join(w for w in (head, note, rest) if w), width), "warn" if note else "bold")


def cut(s, n):
    s = str(s)
    return s if len(s) <= n else s[:max(0, n - 1)] + "…"


def session_line(s, width):
    ctx = f"{s['ctx_pct']}%" if s.get("ctx_pct") is not None else ""
    since = ago(s["since_s"]) if s.get("since_s") is not None else ""
    where = f"{s['repo']}/{s['track']}" if s.get("track") else s.get("repo") or ""
    tone = {"waiting": "warn", "idle": "dim"}.get(s["state"], "")
    return (f"  {cut(s['name'], 24):<24} {cut(where, 28):<28} {s['state']:<8}{since:>5} {ctx:>4}"[:width], tone)


def worker_line(w, width):
    st = {"live": f"live {ago(w['moved_s'])}" if w.get("moved_s") is not None else "live",
          "session": "session", "held": "held", "offline": "OFFLINE"}[w["live"]]
    tone = {"offline": "bad", "held": "dim"}.get(w["live"], "")
    return (f"  {cut(w['repo'] + '/' + w['track'], 34):<34} {st:<10} {w['title']}"[:width], tone)


def home(p, width=80, rows=24):
    """(lines, items) of the main screen: the header, NEEDS YOU, sessions and workers, the landing lane, in `rows`
    lines (the caller's footer is the last of them). lines are (text, tone), tone one of "", dim, warn, bad; items
    are (line, target) for the cursor, target ("session", id) or ("worker", repo, track); a section's items may
    also be ("landing", repo, pr) or ("section", "project", repo)."""
    g = p.get("glance") or {}
    out, items = header(p, width=width), []
    nd, note = p.get("needs") or [], stale_note(p, "needs")
    if nd:
        n = nd[0]
        out.append((cut(f"NEEDS YOU {len(nd)} · " + (f"{note} · " if note else "") + f"{n['repo']} {n['name']}: {n['ask']}",
                        width), "bad"))
    else:
        out.append((cut(f"needs you: nothing  {note}", width) if note else "needs you: nothing", "warn" if note else "dim"))
    ss, wk = p.get("sessions") or [], p.get("workers") or []
    gs, gw, gl = g.get("sessions") or {}, g.get("workers") or {}, g.get("landing") or {}
    room = max(2, rows - len(out) - 4 - (not wk))  # two block headers, the landing line, the footer, and the
                                                   # "(no row marked running)" line when there are no workers
    want_w = len(wk)
    kw = min(want_w, max(room // 2, room - len(ss)))
    ks = room - kw
    if len(ss) > ks:
        ks -= 1                                    # the "+N more" line
    if len(wk) > kw:
        kw -= 1
    out.append(block_head(p, "sessions", f"SESSIONS {len(ss)}",
                          " · ".join(f"{gs.get(w, 0)} {w}" for w in ("waiting", "busy", "idle") if gs.get(w)), width))
    for s in ss[:max(0, ks)]:
        items.append((len(out), ("session", s["id"])))
        out.append(session_line(s, width))
    if len(ss) > max(0, ks):
        rest = ss[max(0, ks):]
        idle = sum(1 for s in rest if s["state"] == "idle")
        out.append((f"  +{len(rest)} more ({idle} idle)   s lists them", "dim"))
    out.append(block_head(p, "workers", f"WORKERS {len(wk)}",
                          " · ".join(f"{gw.get(w, 0)} {w}" for w in ("live", "offline", "held") if gw.get(w)), width))
    for w in wk[:max(0, kw)]:
        items.append((len(out), ("worker", w["repo"], w["track"])))
        out.append(worker_line(w, width))
    if len(wk) > max(0, kw):
        out.append((f"  +{len(wk) - max(0, kw)} more   w lists them", "dim"))
    if not wk:
        out.append(("  (no row marked running)", "dim"))
    if "landing" not in (p.get("sections") or {}):
        out.append(("LANDING reading…", "dim"))
    else:
        head = block_head(p, "landing", "LANDING", f"{gl.get('active', 0)} active · {gl.get('queued', 0)} queued · "
                          f"{gl.get('landed_1h', 0)} landed in 1 h", width)
        out.append((head[0], head[1] if head[1] == "warn" else ""))
    return out[:max(1, rows - 1)], [i for i in items if i[0] < rows - 1]


def section(p, name, width=80, arg=None, now=None):
    """(lines, items) of one tier-2 section, from the pulse alone: sessions, workers, landing, needs, recent,
    projects, box, or project (arg: the repo)."""
    now, out, items = now or time.time(), [], []
    if name == "sessions":
        out.append(block_head(p, "sessions", f"SESSIONS {len(p.get('sessions') or [])}, waiting first", "", width))
        for s in p.get("sessions") or []:
            items.append((len(out), ("session", s["id"])))
            out.append(session_line(s, width))
        if (p["glance"].get("members") or {}).get("sessions"):
            out.append((f"  and {p['glance']['members']['sessions']} in members' workspaces", "dim"))
    elif name == "workers":
        out.append(block_head(p, "workers", f"WORKERS {len(p.get('workers') or [])}", "(board rows marked running)",
                              width))
        for w in p.get("workers") or []:
            items.append((len(out), ("worker", w["repo"], w["track"])))
            out.append(worker_line(w, width))
    elif name == "landing":
        out.append(block_head(p, "landing", "LANDING (in flight, newest first)",
                              " Enter opens a job · P lists what landed · g graphs it", width))
        for x in p.get("landing") or []:
            items.append((len(out), ("landing", x["repo"], str(x["pr"]))))
            out.append((cut(f"  {x['repo']}#{x['pr']:<6} {x['stage']:<9} {ago(x['age_s']):>4}  {x['title']}", width),
                        "bad" if "fail" in x["stage"] else ""))
        if not p.get("landing"):
            out.append(("  (queue empty)", "dim"))
    elif name == "needs":
        out.append(block_head(p, "needs", f"NEEDS YOU {len(p.get('needs') or [])}", "", width))
        for n in p.get("needs") or []:
            out.append((cut(f"  {n['kind']:<8} {n['repo']} {n['name']}: {n['ask']}", width), "warn"))
        if (p["glance"].get("members") or {}).get("needs"):
            out.append((f"  and {p['glance']['members']['needs']} in members' workspaces", "dim"))
    elif name == "recent":
        out.append(("RECENT (24 h of hand-offs and landings, newest first)   r again: the full timeline (T)", "bold"))
        for e in p.get("recent") or []:
            out.append((cut(f"  {time.strftime('%H:%M', time.localtime(e['at']))}  {e['what']:<10} "
                            f"{e['repo']}/{e['name']}  {e['title']}", width), ""))
    elif name == "projects":
        out.append((f"{'PROJECT':<22} {'live':>4} {'run':>4} {'open':>5} {'needs':>5} {'landed':>7} {'$ today':>8}  panel",
                    "bold"))
        for r in p.get("projects") or []:
            items.append((len(out), ("section", "project", r["repo"])))
            out.append((f"  {cut(r['repo'], 20):<20} {r['live']:>4} {r['running']:>4} {r['open']:>5} {r['needs']:>5} "
                        f"{ago(now - r['landed_at']) if r['landed_at'] else '-':>7} "
                        f"{'%.0f' % r['usd'] if r['usd'] is not None else '-':>8}  {'yes' if r['panel'] else ''}",
                        "warn" if r["needs"] else ""))
        m = p["glance"].get("members") or {}
        out.append((f"  members: {m.get('workspaces', 0)} workspaces, {m.get('sessions', 0)} sessions, "
                    f"{m.get('rows', 0)} open rows (counts only)", "dim"))
    elif name == "project":
        r = next((x for x in p.get("projects") or [] if x["repo"] == arg), None)
        if not r:
            return [(f"{arg}: no such project on the pulse", "warn")], []
        out.append((f"{arg}  {r['live']} live · {r['running']} running · {r['open']} open · {r['needs']} need you", "bold"))
        pn = (p.get("panels") or {}).get(arg)
        if pn:
            age = f"{ago(now - pn['at'])} old" if pn.get("at") else "no time"
            out.append((f"PANEL {pn['title']}  ({age}{', STALE' if pn['stale'] else ''})" if not pn["err"]
                        else f"PANEL: {pn['err']}", "warn" if pn["err"] or pn["stale"] else "bold"))
            for row in pn["rows"]:
                out.append((f"  {row['label']:<24} {row['value']}",
                             "dim" if pn["stale"] else {"bad": "bad", "warn": "warn"}.get(row["state"], "")))
        for w in p.get("workers") or []:
            if w["repo"] == arg:
                items.append((len(out), ("worker", w["repo"], w["track"])))
                out.append(worker_line(w, width))
        for s in p.get("sessions") or []:
            if s["repo"] == arg:
                items.append((len(out), ("session", s["id"])))
                out.append(session_line(s, width))
        out.append(("  b opens its board rows", "dim"))
    elif name == "box":
        b = p["glance"].get("box") or {}
        out.append(("BOX", "bold"))
        out += [(f"  {k:<11} {b.get(k)}", "") for k in ("load1", "cores", "mem_pct", "disk_pct", "temp_c", "units_down")]
        lap = (p["glance"].get("laptop") or "(not asked yet)").splitlines() or ["(not asked yet)"]
        out += [(f"  {'laptop' if i == 0 else '':<11} {ln}", "") for i, ln in enumerate(lap)]
        out.append(("SECTIONS (when each last collected, and its error)", "bold"))
        for k, v in sorted((p.get("sections") or {}).items()):
            out.append((f"  {k:<10} {ago(now - v['at']) + ' ago' if v.get('at') else 'never':<10} {v.get('err') or ''}",
                        "bad" if v.get("err") else ""))
    return out, items


def text(p, width=80, rows=24):
    lines, _ = home(p, width, rows)
    return "\n".join(t for t, _ in lines)


def main(argv):
    if argv[:1] == ["selfcheck"]:
        return selfcheck()
    if argv[:1] == ["--once"] and argv[1:] in (["--json"], ["--text"]):
        p = Pulse().step(laptop=False)
        if argv[1] == "--json":
            print(json.dumps(p, indent=1))
        else:
            print(text(p))
        return 0
    if argv[:1] == ["run"]:
        out = argv[2] if argv[1:2] == ["--out"] and len(argv) > 2 else None
        try:
            feed(lambda p: write(p, out), out=out)
        except KeyboardInterrupt:
            pass
        return 0
    print(__doc__.split("\n\n")[2], file=sys.stderr)
    return 2


# ── selfcheck ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
SHAPE = {"v": int, "at": int, "zone": str, "host": str, "glance": dict, "sessions": list, "workers": list,
         "landing": list, "needs": list, "recent": list, "projects": list, "panels": dict, "sections": dict}
GLANCE = {"needs": ("n",), "sessions": ("busy", "waiting", "idle", "shell"),
          "workers": ("live", "offline", "held"), "landing": ("active", "queued", "landed_1h"),
          "box": ("load1", "cores", "mem_pct", "disk_pct", "temp_c", "units_down"),
          "members": ("workspaces", "sessions", "rows", "needs")}
ROWS = {"sessions": ("id", "name", "repo", "track", "state", "since_s", "ctx_pct", "win"),
        "workers": ("repo", "track", "title", "status", "live", "moved_s", "held"),
        "landing": ("repo", "pr", "stage", "title", "age_s"), "needs": ("kind", "repo", "name", "ask"),
        "recent": ("at", "what", "repo", "name", "title"),
        "projects": ("repo", "live", "running", "open", "needs", "landed_at", "usd", "panel")}


def valid(p):
    """[problem] where p departs from THE SHAPE; empty when it matches."""
    bad = [f"{k} missing or not {t.__name__}" for k, t in SHAPE.items() if not isinstance(p.get(k), t)]
    g = p.get("glance") or {}
    for k, fields in GLANCE.items():
        bad += [f"glance.{k}.{f} missing" for f in fields if f not in (g.get(k) or {})]
    bad += [f"glance.{k} missing" for k in ("limit_until", "model", "laptop", "spend_today") if k not in g]
    for k, fields in ROWS.items():
        for i, r in enumerate(p.get(k) or []):
            bad += [f"{k}[{i}].{f} missing" for f in fields if f not in r]
    for repo, pn in (p.get("panels") or {}).items():
        bad += [f"panels.{repo}.{f} missing" for f in ("title", "at", "rows", "stale", "err") if f not in pn]
    return bad


def selfcheck(*a, **k):
    """The cases are core/tests/selfcheck/cc-pulse.py, run in THIS namespace so their stubs and `global`
    rebinds land on the tool as they did when the body was here. Defining them replaces this selfcheck()."""
    path = os.path.join(os.path.dirname(os.path.dirname(os.path.realpath(__file__))), "tests", "selfcheck", "cc-pulse.py")
    with open(path, encoding="utf-8") as fh:
        exec(compile(fh.read(), path, "exec"), globals())
    return globals()["selfcheck"](*a, **k)


if __name__ == "__main__":
    sys.exit(main(sys.argv[1:]))
